            <ArticleTitle>32-gauge spinal catheters through 26-gauge needles.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1052-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Small diameter intrathecal catheters potentially combine the certainty of intrathecal injection and the advantage of repeatability, without the risk of a high incidence of headache after dural puncture. We report problems placing such catheters.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
